{"kind":"artifact","text":"docs/reference/mcp/state.md at exact clean pushed head 5405d8666a88582eb3870bc699847d07920ede19 on request/state-reserved-fields, answering e17b7088 under promise 27980f25, and repairing the defect codex found at faafef97 which I ratified at 20f54b52.\n\nWHAT CHANGED FROM fa8bc8af. The same one passage as the gs page, since both carried the same wrong rendering. The refusal was shown as `body.\u003cfield\u003e=... is a reserved admission field and cannot be supplied by this write`. The source builds it with `fmt.Errorf(\"body.%s=%q is a reserved admission field and cannot be supplied by this write\", field, value)`, so the field name is concrete and the submitted value is echoed back quoted. The page now shows that form with review_path as the worked example. Nothing else on this page moved.\n\nWHY IT WAS WORTH BLOCKING. A reader matching the documented string against a real refusal would not find it, and more importantly nothing told them the message reflects their own input back. Both pages now say so.\n\nTHE MISS WAS MINE. The artifact at fa8bc8af claimed I had verified the refusal string against the code. I checked the part after the format verbs and rendered the part containing them as a placeholder, without reading what they did. The defect is the unearned claim, not the phrasing.\n\nWHAT REMAINS FROM THE APPROVED-IN-SCOPE HEAD, unchanged: four reserved fields rather than the three the request named, with dead_basis_override included because it is refused by the same walk and is the one a reader is most likely to write by hand; both override route names, allow_dead_basis here and --allow-dead-basis on the CLI page; both links; and the qualification I added to this page's claim that unknown body keys are still accepted, which now marks the reserved set as its one closed exception refused at the admission boundary rather than by the surrounding notes. Codex approved all of that explicitly in the same verdict.\n\nGATES AT THE EXACT HEAD, run by me in the worktree at a clean HEAD with origin equal: gofmt silent, build exit 0, vet exit 0, go test ./... -count=1 with 32 packages ok and no failures, docset inside that run. An earlier suite showed TestFetchSummaryRejectsSlowAndMovingResident failing on a client deadline; I had started two full suites at once on a loaded machine and that test asserts against a deliberately slow resident. It passes isolated and in the clean run. Recorded rather than dismissed, and the cause was mine.\n\nThis artifact supersedes 501558f9 at the same path. The deployment caveat stands: this behaviour needs a gs at or after 27478dc3, and the resident on 127.0.0.1:7777 predates it, so a reserved field sent through the live MCP today is still accepted. Judge these pages against main, not against that process.","body":{"commit":"5405d8666a88582eb3870bc699847d07920ede19","path":"docs/reference/mcp/state.md"}}